{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"submission_c1.json\",\"summary\":\"First Candidate (action=obligation) plus a 2-object map extension, validated clean (valid=True, no diagnostics).\\n\\nSourced discrepancy investigated: ConfigurationStore documents that StoreConfiguration(index, configuration) 'is invoked once a log entry containing a configuration change is committed' (configuration.go:44-52), but the only call site is inside applySingle (fsm.go:118), and runFSM only reaches applySingle when the FSM does NOT implement BatchingFSM (fsm.go:127-186). BatchingFSM.ApplyBatch separately documents that LogConfiguration entries 'will be sent' to the batching FSM (fsm.go:51-69). A FSM implementing both interfaces therefore never receives StoreConfiguration, and the library's own batchtest helper (testing_batch.go:17-33) returns nil for non-LogCommand entries, consistent with the gap rather than with the ConfigurationStore contract.\\n\\nProduct contents:\\n- Obligation claim-config-store-delivery: for every FSM implementing ConfigurationStore, the library must invoke StoreConfiguration for each committed configuration entry it delivers to the FSM.\\n- One question grounded on the new principal Fact f-fsm-configuration-state (A6) with direct Behavior b-fsm-apply-committed, lifecycle=establishment, and the A1 tie declared through supporting behavior b-append-entries-sync (the configuration fact consumed by AppendEntries is the same configuration whose FSM-side persistence is at issue).\\n- One physical binding (symbol runFSM, fsm.go:86-125) with a single association across S34-S38.\\n- Retained counterevidence and unknowns: the deliberate early return at fsm.go:111-115; ApplyBatch's doc implying batching FSMs are expected to persist configuration themselves (so this may be an imprecise interface comment rather than an incomplete dispatch); and no existing test combining BatchingFSM with ConfigurationStore. No violation is asserted; the discriminator (does StoreConfiguration get called for a committed config entry when the FSM implements both interfaces?) is deferred to the next-turn direct check.\\n- Map extension: new Behavior b-fsm-apply-committed (A5) and Fact f-fsm-configuration-state (A6), plus a high-consequence deferred Surface recording the discrepancy. No previously accepted object was modified or removed.\"}"}}
